 "notes": "Solo-act recovery for the Shore/Morris (census_shore_morris.json) and South Jersey (census_south_jersey.json) crawls. Rule used: a solo act is kept only when the same venue lists a band on the same date (census or raw), or when the venue is a park/concert series or festival. Porchfests (Asbury Park, Red Bank, Moorestown, Magnolia) were skipped entirely. The window is 2025-01-01 to 2026-12-31, matching the census.\nRaw sources read: raw.tsv (the crawl's parsed titles for Asbury Park Brewery, Bar Anticipation and The Homestead; per-event URLs reused); the apboardwalk.com show feed copies (apb.json live, apb64/apb_64e0ba/wbj_20260623235353, apb_038747/wbj_20260415122012, apb_old/apb_05a072/apball_1007, wbj_20250930132717) for Wonder Bar, Low Dive, Palmetto and the Stone Pony; Stone Pony Wayback snapshots sm/sp_*.html; Tim McLoone's sm/tm_*.html (including the gzipped Jul 2025 copy); Autodidact sm/au_*.html and auto.html; Fort Nonsense fne.html; Tonewood tw.html; Pier Village pv.json/pv.tsv; Moorestown mtc.html; Gallagher's x.html. South Jersey has no raw files: that crawl couldn't reach Wayback and built its rows from press/aggregator snippets, so the only raw bill text is the billing field in census_south_jersey.json (and the same strings in its build script sj.py). The solo openers named there were recovered.\nVenues with nothing recoverable: The Homestead (its solo nights (Mikey Gee, Jimmy Vivino, Tom Hamilton, Sam Bush, Porter Martin, Brandon Niederauer) were all on nights with no band); Tim McLoone's (one act per night; solo nights like Bob Egan, Molly McGuire and Sharon Lasher had no band); Autodidact (no solo shared a band night; 'Luke Mattessich + Tommy Hyde (The Living Dogs)' is the band itself); Fort Nonsense; Tonewood; Low Dive and Palmetto ('Francis Doom + Friends' and 'Dead Frequency with Tyler Valentine & Pepe Loco' skipped as unclear). Raw files weren't saved for McLoone's Pier House (the Pier Village feed text is cut off before the lineup; the census rows came from a hand-made list), Moorestown Summer Concerts (Google Sheet), Jamian's, The Vogel, Asbury Lanes, Union Firehouse, Morristown Jazz & Blues and Haddon Township Summer of Love. Their solo acts couldn't be recovered. The same goes for the South Jersey park-series solo headliners, whose names weren't kept.\nJudgement calls: (1) At the Stone Pony, solos were added only on bills of local or regional bands, because the census leaves the Pony's national touring shows out on purpose. Openers on national-only bills were left out, e.g. Kami Kehoe, Josh Heinrichs (Fortunate Youth), Spencer LaJoye, Margaret Glaspy, Jesse Malin with Hollis Brown and Belle Blue, and Kenny Whitmire. Wonder Bar solos on national bills were kept, because the census itself lists those Wonder Bar bands. (2) Single-word or unclear stage names were skipped as possibly bands: Mønte, Monte Maybe, Jwalttz, Love Seat Pete, St. Germaine, Trichor, Pronto, Diva Bleach, Lolitslea, Chousand, Raw Milk, Erly, Errth, Noop, Calundronius, Mxtchll, Brunsy, Lavelle, jm cooks, Eefah, LNJ Sessions, Love James, Anthony'2, Miss Ohio, Best Bear and Bren (Haddon Lake Park), Laylow Jones and Los Gringo (Bar A Dylan night), and Sports on the Radio (the census leaves it out at APB but counts it as a band at the Wonder Bar). Duos (Kane & James, Maddie Freeman & Sam Feldman, Briscoe) were skipped. (3) Acts inside a band's billing were skipped: Elliot Lurie with Yacht Rock Gold, Cat Manning starring in Just Like Janis, Ed Lover presenting the Live Mixtape Band, and Palmyra Delran 'and her band'. (4) The Bar A spellings 'GREG AULDEN' (2025) and 'GREG ALDEN' (2026) were merged as Greg Alden. APB's 'Greg McLaughlin' (2026-06-26) was kept apart from 'Gregory McLoughlin' (2026-03-14) because the spellings differ, though they may be the same person. 'Int'l Superstar Robin' was written out as International Superstar Robin. (5) Billy Pontiac ('from Atlantic City Expressway', a guest at the Never Say Goodbye show) and Jeff Kazee (with Adam Ezra Group) were kept as solo guests. On 2026-08-07, 2026-10-26, 2026-11-06 and 2026-12-04 the Wonder Bar bands (Adam Ezra Group; Forced to Joust/Shriek/Milk Street; Never Say Goodbye; American Girlfriend) are in the raw feed but not in the census on those dates. (6) The Chris Kirkpatrick and Ryan Cabrera (Pop 2000s Tour), Joan Osborne and Kevin Devine rows are national names. They're kept because the venue is a concert series or the bill has a band. (7) APB per-event URLs are the crawl's Squarespace links as saved; a few slugs don't match the date (e.g. Nick Clemons 2025-08-26 links /2025/7/26/...), which is how the site reuses them. source_type follows the census listing ('press' for the South Jersey park-series announcements)."
